# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_draft_branch_lane_leak.py" "DRAFT BRANCH-LANE LEAK GATE: PASS" "draft branch-lane leak (a draft PR closed-unmerged without ever being marked ready must NOT strand its head branch's push-time BR-<head> lane -- a phantom in-flight that inflates contention forever)" "draft branch-lane leak: a feature-branch push reserves lanes before any PR under BR-<head>. A draft PR can close before push-to-PR reconciliation, so the close handler must also release the head branch reservation. The release is idempotent for non-draft and draft-to-ready paths. Proven through the real event processor with GitHub I/O faked: abandoned drafts leave no live lane or phantom contention, ordinary close and merge paths still converge, and a later push can reserve the branch again. Content-free and never-crash" "draft branch-lane leak: a closed PR releases its head branch's push-time BR-<head> lane so an abandoned draft cannot strand phantom contention" 16
